WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:08.099
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Cli-gui turns a command line into a form.

1
00:00:09.419 --> 00:00:14.419
It reads your tool's own parser.
One page, a field for every flag.

2
00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:18.494
Your colleague needs this tool.
They will not open a terminal.

3
00:00:18.659 --> 00:00:22.619
Not that they cannot.
7 flags in order is not an interface.

4
00:00:22.819 --> 00:00:26.900
So you build the form by hand.
Then the tool grows a flag.

5
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.160
So the command writes its own page.
Options become fields, choices a list.

6
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.360
Required stays required.
Every default is already in its box.

7
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.212
The page runs nothing.
Your browser assembles the exact line.

8
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.400
It reads the parser your tool built.
Not prose about that parser.

9
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.212
argparse and Click are walked directly;
a Typer application is already Click.

10
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.000
What it cannot import,
it reads off that tool's own help screen.

11
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.320
A page that silently drops a
flag looks entirely correct.

12
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.700
So it checks the page against the parser.
Each rule names what you lose.

13
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.875
This is docker. Written in Go,
and not importable from Python.

14
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.160
Its help screen came out as 57 sections
and 1,307 form fields, in one pass.

15
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.840
And git comes out empty.
Its section titles are prose.

16
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.320
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.399
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
